A||||3||fiero56||test drive||||10||
Z||000000||fiero56||05-06-2000||10:03 PM||||After going "yarding" this morning, I decided to head over to one of the local Lexus dealerships and check out an NSX that had been sitting in their lot for the last week or so.  Was talking with the sales guy, asked him if he could open it up, start the engine and let me hear it. He handed me the keys, and let me look over the car. <BR>First glance, the roof line on the NSX is quite a bit lower than my Fiero. Several good sized inches. Doors are quite a bit lighter than Fieros. Take little force to throw them open. NSX seats sit right about the same height as the Fiero. Quite a bit less horizontal foot room in the NSX, much less(almost no dead pedal). Clutch is a tad lighter than my Fieros. Shifter felt nice, but throws are longer than I thought they would be. Much less head room, I am 6' and I was almost hitting the roof line(plain roof <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">).  <BR>Weeeelllll, the guy let me take it out for a spin. NSX has the Honda DOHC v-tec engine. Around town, it pulls no stronger than my Formula Fiero. I was beginning to get bored with the lackluster acceleration. Finally found an open road out of town. I decided to run the engine up a ways. It was doing normal, then when 4,500rpm came up, it threw me in the seat HARD. Felt like a supercharger just kicked in and gave the car another 200hp.  VERY nice.<BR>The NSX feels very solid. Even more than my Fiero. There is NO BODY ROLL at all, even with the slightly softer ride than my fiero. Handling is also nicer than my Fiero. Corners are taken even faster in this car.<P>Cons. Around town driving, the NSX is somewhat of a bore. No low end torue at all. The clutch is a little wierd. There is NO feedback at all. Shifter throws are a little long for $50,000(the Miata has a better shifting tranny). Very little trunk room in back. No storage room in front at all. Exhaust has that stupid small displacement engine sound(nothing like the Fiero sound).<P>Pros. VERY fast once the engine winds up. Cornering/handling is better than Fiero. Seater are very nice. Good stereo.<P>I like the looks of the NSX over the fiero. But, I would stay with my Fiero. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||RiceCooker||05-06-2000||10:29 PM||||DEFINITELY THE FIERO!!!<P>- Imagine what you could do to a fiero with the amount of $$$ the NSX costs. <P>- Definitely a wicked sleeper to suprise those other fancy imports.<P>- Still got the pride of owning america's only made and *THE WORLD'S BEST* mid-engined sports car (Ferrari 355 is close)||||reg||4
Z||000002||Raydar||05-07-2000||10:09 AM||||When the NSX first appeared, there were several journalists who complained about its "lack of soul", because it was so refined. Said it felt like a very fast Accord. <BR>I've never driven one, so I can't comment, first hand. <BR>That 4500 RPM rush is what happens when V-TEC kicks in.   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||05-08-2000||02:17 AM||||56,<P>:P I see how you are!  Ditch the white-trash yarding buddy and head out to drive a NSX.  <P>I used to work for that dealership indirectly too.  You are so young my son, so much to learn.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||2
